    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, please have a seat. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S005",
      "patient_response": "Well, thank you for seeing me. I, um... I came in because I just can't seem to get anything in order anymore. It's like everything is slipping through my fingers. You see, my kitchen table—which used to be where we'd have our nice Sunday breakfasts, just me and my husband—is completely covered now. I mean, you can't even see the wood underneath. It's just piles and piles of his medical appointment papers, because he's been having some trouble with his knee, and then there are all these church flyers for the bake sale and the choir schedule, and notes from the senior center about the Tuesday bingo and the Wednesday walking group... and all these half-finished lists I make. I write them thinking, \"Okay, this will help,\" but I only get halfway through before I lose my train of thought. So I just sit there at the table, looking at all of it, and I honestly don't know which thing to do first. I pick up a paper, put it down, look at another one... and before I know it, the whole day is gone. Just gone. And I haven't accomplished a single thing. It's so frustrating because I feel like I should be able to handle this, but I just sit there paralyzed by it all.",
